    "demoHeading": "SharedMap sudoku cells, live",
    "demoCopy": [
      "Three watershed documents run the full runtime in your browser, wire codecs and pending queues included. The runtime is compiled to JavaScript. They talk to one sluice: the in-memory server that ships in the library, standing in for floodgate with no backend. A cell edit renders optimistically and pushes an op the sluice sequences; delivery is explicit, so state propagates one stamped hop at a time. Local edits are drawn in magenta until the sequencer stamps them; server-sequenced state is ink.",
      "Click any cell to cycle its digit, type 1–9 to write directly, or press Delete or Shift-click to clear. Arrow keys move across each board. Press Race the same cell and A, B, and C write different digits to the center cell, r4c4, at the same instant. The sluice sequences those writes FIFO, and every replica converges on the last sequenced value."
    ],
